Rule narrowing: the PM replaced the any-depth rule with a contiguous-block rule. FR-1 through FR-3 now state that an open box is ignored only when it sits directly under a non-deferred [x] line in one contiguous checkbox block. A plain item, a heading, a blank line, a deferred line, a [b] line, or a same-or-shallower indent line ends the block. A nested [x] needs its own SHA unless its direct [x] parent in the block covers it. The skip-ignored coverage lookup is gone. No ignored chain remains. [b] and deferred boundary handling from rounds 1 and 2 stays unchanged.

Math fixture: tests/spec_review_gate/fixtures/math_real_plan.md is a verbatim read-only copy of Math's plan. The fixture test builds its expected feedback from itemized line numbers, not pinned totals. The narrow rule gives 40 'plan task is not complete' lines and 71 'completed plan task lacks commit SHA' lines. Of the 35 nested 'not complete' lines, 26 sit under four top-level open manual-verification parents (L148-153, L273-279, L395-401, L491-496) and 9 sit after the plain list item at L261 (L262-270). These are genuine open tasks of Math's plan that Math must tick or defer. The other nested [ ] lines yield no 'not complete' line. The Math plan is not fully covered by this fix; the Overview, README, and CHANGELOG state that fact.

